SUMMARY:Preserving National History Locally: Tour of the Petaluma Woman’s Club
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Petaluma Woman’s Club’s recent addition to the National Register of Historic Places.\nDate:  Wednesday May 27\, 5:00-6:30 PM\nVenue: Petaluma Woman’s Club\n518 B Street\nPetaluma\, CA 94952\nCost:  Free\nPlease RSVP Here\n \nAs a part of National Historic Preservation Month festivities\, the Petaluma Woman’s Club invites you to a special event in celebration of its recent designation on the National Register of Historic Places. The program will feature a presentation by local historians and current Club members on the history of the Petaluma Woman’s Club\, including its role in the broader Women’s Club movement. The presentation will be followed by a guided tour of the historic 1913 Craftsman-style building\, designed by notable local architect Brainerd Jones.
URL:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/calendar-event/preserving-national-history-locally-tour-of-the-petaluma-womans-club/
LOCATION:Petaluma Woman’s Club\, 518 B Street\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952\, United States
CATEGORIES:Event,History Trails Walks,NHPM
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.petalumamuseum.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/womans-club-1a.jpg
END:VEVENT
